From c923c024030a47e166cbe58507c403abd7b2e465 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:08:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 63/63] bluetooth: HID devices, and a sturdier stack to carry
 them

Bluetooth keyboards, mice and gamepads work like USB ones: the new
bluetooth_hid driver, the HID host profile in bluetooth_server, the
fixes to the kernel stack, libbluetooth and the server that a link
needs from pairing to disconnection, the setup of the controllers
when they are opened, scripting, and the Bluetooth and Input
preferences.

The same work is proposed to RenkuOS as a series of pull requests,
starting with #252.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
